        "texts": {
          "summary": "100 × TodoItem (memo) re-render on every step: prop `onToggle` is a new function each render with the same value, passed at TodoApp.tsx:29; `handleToggle` is declared at TodoApp.tsx:9. Wasted: about 10.1 ms per step. Fix: wrap `handleToggle` in useCallback (React Compiler would do this automatically).",
          "why": "memo only skips a render when every prop is the same object as last time. `onToggle` looks the same, but it's a new function on every render, so TodoItem re-renders for nothing.",
          "line": "`onToggle={handleToggle}` at TodoApp.tsx:29. `handleToggle` is declared at TodoApp.tsx:9: `function handleToggle(id: number) { … }`.",
          "fix": "Wrap `handleToggle` (declared at TodoApp.tsx:9) in useCallback so TodoItem gets the same function until its dependencies change: `const handleToggle = useCallback((id: number) => { … }, []);`, keeping its body. The dependency list can stay empty: it only calls `setTodos`, with an updater (`setTodos((prev) => …)`), so it never reads the current state, and a state setter never changes. React Compiler would do this automatically."
        },
        "rank": 1
      }
